{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791282544,"nonce":"bWCx+LSdg7c4/bxTTmPgPZNmFUk=","title":"Strip-mined loops that call natives hold off a world stop for seconds","message":"A compiled loop polls once per strip of 256 iterations (ASH_STRIP_MINE). That assumes cheap iterations. A loop whose body calls a long native -- here `hl.Bytes.fill` over 256 MB, a few ms each -- reaches its poll only every 256 calls, so a world stop waits for the whole strip:\n\n    [gc] world stop waiting 25.0ms on 1 of 10 mutators: os-worker 0x16e81f0e0\n    [gc]   os-worker 0x16e81f0e0 is at: platform_memset \u003c- (jit) \u003c- (jit) \u003c- ash_static_call \u003c- hlp_call_method \u003c- hlp_jit_closure_runner \u003c- ...run_closure_body \u003c- ...fiber_run\n    [gc] world stopped after 1337.4ms\n\nReproducer (hybrid, ASH_GC_STATS=1 ASH_GC_COLLECT_AT_REFILLS=every:50):\n\n    var big = new hl.Bytes(1 \u003c\u003c 28);\n    Thread.create(() -\u003e for (i in 0...400) big.fill(0, 1 \u003c\u003c 28, i));\n    // main thread allocates in a loop\n\nThe interpreter, which polls every iteration, never waits over 20 ms on the same program. Options: do not strip-mine a loop whose body contains a call (or a native call), or poll after every call in a strip-mined body.","files":null}]}